#: pybroker.optimize.OptimizeMixin.optimize:1
msgid ""
"Searches :func:`pybroker.optimize.hyperparam` values on a training "
"window, then evaluates the best values on the held out test window."
msgstr ""

#: ce501ad5514d42ccbc3d236673d8f93d of
#: pybroker.optimize.OptimizeMixin.optimize:4
msgid ""
"Data supplied by the :class:`pybroker.data.DataSource` is split into "
"train and test as specified by ``train_size``. Every trial backtests the "
"train window with one combination of hyperparameter values and scores it "
"with ``score_fn``. The winning combination is then replayed on the test "
"window, which ``score_fn`` never sees."
msgstr ""

#: 456f527c32f94748a8fba6679dd7b680 of
#: pybroker.optimize.OptimizeMixin.optimize:10
msgid ""
"Pretrained models (``model(..., pretrained=True)``) are loaded per train "
"window and reused across that window's trials. Trainable models are not "
"supported; tune them inside ``train_fn`` with a validation split, or use "
":meth:`pybroker.strategy.Strategy.walkforward`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/pybroker.optimize.rst
#: 197414084eae4623a457698d0853c6f0 7c33934037614f9dac7a03121329aa63
#: ef1ff8d6901d48ec884603f8771b05eb
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: c6a7c07d80c445c68996cd2e8ee09b05 of
#: pybroker.optimize.OptimizeMixin.optimize:15
msgid ""
"``Callable[[TestResult], float]`` that scores one trial's train window "
"backtest. Maximized by default; see ``direction``."
msgstr ""

#: d3de815863eb41df920fd5fac4aa9128 of
#: pybroker.optimize.OptimizeMixin.optimize:17
msgid ""
"How candidate values are chosen. ``\"grid\"`` (the default) exhaustively "
"enumerates every combination, ``\"tpe\"`` uses "
":class:`optuna.samplers.TPESampler`, ``\"random\"`` uses "
":class:`optuna.samplers.RandomSampler`. An "
":class:`optuna.samplers.BaseSampler` instance is also accepted; it is "
"deep-copied and re-seeded per window, and a multi-window run ships copies"
" to worker processes, so it must be picklable. Grid and random samplers "
"evaluate trials in parallel on the configured workers. Any other sampler "
"— ``\"tpe\"``, or an instance that is not a "
":class:`~optuna.samplers.GridSampler` or "
":class:`~optuna.samplers.RandomSampler` — is adaptive, and evaluating its"
" trials in batches would change the values it proposes and tie results to"
" the worker count; its trials therefore run sequentially, and an info-"
"level log message notes that parallelism was disabled."
msgstr ""

#: 83be6c03af414f1ba3ccd862eaf37920 of
#: pybroker.optimize.OptimizeMixin.optimize:33
msgid ""
"Number of trials to run. Required for every sampler except ``\"grid\"``, "
"where it defaults to the full grid size and a smaller value samples that "
"many combinations at random."
msgstr ""

#: 78621f0380e84ebaa9afb0754907e92d of
#: pybroker.optimize.OptimizeMixin.optimize:36
msgid "``\"maximize\"`` (default) or ``\"minimize\"`` ``score_fn``."
msgstr ""

#: 358da94cc34241f8b307081fb344a62b of
#: pybroker.optimize.OptimizeMixin.optimize:37
msgid ""
"Random seed for the sampler and for bootstrap metrics. Defaults to "
"``None``, which does not reproduce."
msgstr ""

#: 67ffc3bffbc74659be82aad0f49ea89f of
#: pybroker.optimize.OptimizeMixin.optimize:39
msgid ""
"When greater than ``1``, hyperparameters are optimized separately in each"
" of ``windows`` walkforward windows and the test windows are stitched "
"into one continuous result. Defaults to ``None``, a single train/test "
"split."
msgstr ""

#: 303beec5f596412dbe4fff295226490e of
#: pybroker.optimize.OptimizeMixin.optimize:43
msgid ""
"Existing :class:`optuna.study.Study` to record trials in, for example one"
" backed by persistent storage. The study's own sampler and pruner are "
"used, and its direction must match ``direction``. Not supported when "
"``windows`` is greater than ``1``."
msgstr ""

#: d592ba441be44f46bff989fe08ed4a84 of
#: pybroker.optimize.OptimizeMixin.optimize:48
msgid ""
